## Decisions of the orchestrator, recorded

- D-P11-1: the 3 right columns of the A3 cover PNGs (x 4958 to 4960) are the Chrome sub-pixel seam
  (0.25 mm; the same seam as the accepted F7-6 rule, 1 px at 96 ppi = 0.26 mm). CHECK_13 counts white
  edge rows with no pixel ignored and white edge columns with the outermost 3 px of each side ignored.
  The raw counts are information. One information line shows page 1 of the A3 print file at 150 ppi.
- D-P11-2: page 1 of the A3 readers shows only the top-left 198 x 148.5 mm of the A3 cover, with no
  title plaque and no logo; the rest of the sheet is white while pages 2 and 12 fill the sheet. This is
  a defect, F8 (open). The cause is `readers.ts` line 510: `.reader-page > .quest-cover-picture` has the
  leaf size, but the a3-color cover renders at 420 x 297 mm. F8 is in the old r5 file too, so F7 did
  not cause it. The next Red and Green round fixes it. CHECK_13 checks the F7 scope and passes;
  CHECK_14 checks whole page 1 and fails now.
- D-P11-3 (information, as written): "F7b open: the mirror copies the soft edge rows of the Forge art
  (row 167 at the top, mean 193.7 with 697 light pixels; rows 2831 to 2833 at the bottom, means 98.2,
  88.5, 148.1, against 105.6 for the floor). This leaves a hairline of about 0.2 mm at about 8.5 mm
  from the top and bottom edges of the w01-1 A3 cover. The next round changes the fill to topRows 168
  and bottomRows 169."

